==Mobile and Official Client Improvements==
===Mobile UI Scaling and Scaling Settings Changes===
The mobile client is played across a wide range of screen dimensions - from standard phones to larger tablets. With such variety, along with differing player preferences, many mobile players have asked for greater control over the interface size. In particular, tablet users want to be able to scale down the UI for a more customisable experience.

Following your feedback, we've now added the ability to reduce the UI scale on the Mobile client. You'll find that the default value is 400%, as the Mobile Client defaults to high scale. There's also a magnification cap in place, so the interface never gets too tiny to use.
[[File:Easter 2026 & PvP QoL Improvements (10).png|thumb|400px|center|''If you can’t see the image above, click [https://cdn.runescape.com/assets/img/external/oldschool/2026/Newsposts/2026-03-25/ui.png here]!'']]

Note: Some devices will see no change when moving through the higher values, as depending on your device, the interface will likely have capped at a lower value. We recommend just moving through the values and see what works best for you.

To make the UI scaling interface consistent and easier to use across Mobile and desktop, we've updated it to a drop-down rather than slider on the Official Client as well. On fresh install, the UI Scaling is set the same as the Operating System Display Scale, and if you have a different preference, you can adjust it in the drop-drown in the settings.

We've also added a second option, "Input", which lets you type in valid numbers from the whole range directly. To do this, you need to long-press on the scaling drop down if on mobile, or right-click on desktop and select the "input" option.

===FPS Setting Improvements on the Official Client===

* To give players more control over performance, we’ve added separate “Max Foreground FPS” and “Max Background FPS” settings, allowing the game to run at a lower frame rate while not in focus.

===More Client Changes===
These changes came with yesterday's client update, but we thought we'd do a quick ICYMI!

* Improved behaviour of Audio Sliders so they act more like you'd expect. Previously, having a low Master Volume could result in some audio channels being unintentionally muted.
* '''(Android/PC only)''' Fixed a bug that prevented Anti Aliasing settings appearing on supported devices.

==Sailing Update==
We wanted to share a quick update on further boat combat balancing changes that are currently in progress and scheduled to release next week.

As mentioned on our <u>[https://www.youtube.com/live/Hc9SbKLvuo4?si=3H6A7hpExjpAaiVk Q&amp;A Livestream]</u>, we're applying a buff to cannons when they are actively manned by a player. Take a look at this GIF of it working in action below!
[[File:Easter 2026 & PvP QoL Improvements (11).mp4|thumb|600px|center|''If you can’t see the asset above, click [https://cdn.runescape.com/assets/img/external/oldschool/2026/Newsposts/2026-03-25/videowip.mp4 here]!'']]

Whilst we can't give you exact rates of what's changing yet, our goal is to close the gap between cannons and player gear, ensuring that a player using a cannon is on par to the DPS of traditional combat +2 Crew members using cannons.

We're also going to be reducing sea creature HP, especially for those that are smaller and lower-level, so that they are less tanky and their health is more thematically suitable.

We're also addressing an issue with the player's worn gear not contributing as expected to damage calculations. A fix for this will be included alongside the above changes, ensuring that gear will correctly contribute to your overall damage. 

You’ve given us plenty of great suggestions for further improvements to boat combat. For now, we'd like to see how these changes land before planning any further adjustments, so we can see how these changes affect your gains in practice. Once the update is live, we'll be closely monitoring your feedback, so let us know how it feels when it launches next week.

A huge thank you for all of your feedback and your patience while we work on these changes. Sailing will continue to be shaped by the community, and we really value the hands-on experience from those of you who have jumped in to try it out. While we know there are broader changes you'd like to see for boat combat, we hope these updates demonstrate our commitment to iterating alongside you and creating a better foundation for future expansions. 

Speaking of future expansions, we're also nearly ready to share details on our next expansion to boat combat (NPC Boats). This includes new enemies, new rewards and new cannonballs, so keep an eye out for more information coming soon!

